      <h1 class="mt-4 text-[clamp(2.75rem,4.5vw+1rem,5rem)] leading-[0.98] tracking-[-0.01em] text-balance">A shop for every head on the block</h1>
      <div class="prose-taper mt-8 max-w-[58ch] text-lg text-base-content/80">
        <p>Tasha Greer learned to cut in her uncle's barbershop on Baltimore's west side. Wren Castillo trained in Philadelphia, cutting curls dry, one at a time. In 2019 they took over a former mill office on Mill Row, with tall windows and a floor that creaks by the door, and put in three chairs.</p>
        <p>Two years later they threw out the men's and women's menus. A cut takes the time it takes, and the price should say so: since 2021, every service at Good Side is priced by its chair time and the level of the person cutting, whoever is sitting down.</p>
